※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4593

※ A function with no body is the declaration of one defined somewhere else, and
※ the attribute is what says so.  A function that was meant to have a body is
※ one whose body was left off, and the two read alike until the attribute says
※ which was meant.

fn nowhere() → i64

@[startup, impure]
fn main() → u6:
    if nowhere() = 0i64: 0u6 else: 1u6
